            <ArticleTitle>Treatment of pain in patients with complicating disorders: case report from Norway, with commentaries from Germany and Belgium.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>388-9; discussion 389-90</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3109/15360288.2012.734909</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 70-year-old male with a history of bipolar disorder, alcohol misuse, and polyneuropathy is presented. His treatment was complicated by multiple drugs, and by instability and falls. The advantages and disadvantages and dosing considerations with short- and long-acting analgesics are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
